# Response headers. Contract §5a.
#
# This file is the single source of truth for headers, and it is written in the
# one format both Netlify and Cloudflare Pages read. They used to live in
# netlify.toml, which meant moving host meant rewriting the security policy —
# the last thing that should have to be retyped under time pressure. Now the
# host only supplies a build command.
#
# One rule: a value cannot span lines here, so the CSP is a single long line.
# It is the same policy netlify.toml carried, character for character.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://cdn.sanity.io; media-src 'self' https://cdn.sanity.io; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://aur12nrf.api.sanity.io https://api.web3forms.com; form-action 'self' https://api.web3forms.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Why style-src allows 'unsafe-inline' — a deliberate, recorded deviation from
# the contract's blanket ban. The build emits 173 style attributes, 123 of them
# the base64 blur placeholder each photograph is painted over while it loads.
# Blocking them does not degrade the page, it breaks it: the placeholders
# vanish and the layout attributes go with them. That is not a hypothetical —
# it shipped once, and the whole production site came up unstyled.
#
# style-src-attr would be the precise instrument, permitting attributes while
# keeping <style> elements locked to 'self', but it is not supported everywhere
# and browsers lacking it fall back to style-src and break. The risk accepted is
# CSS injection, which needs an injection point; this site renders no user input
# into any page, and there are zero inline <style> blocks and zero inline
# scripts to aim at.
#
# script-src has no 'unsafe-inline' and no 'unsafe-eval'. The site's only script
# is /scripts/site.js from this origin, and that is the restriction that matters.
#
# form-action and connect-src each allow exactly one outside address,
# api.web3forms.com, because the enquiry form now posts there from the
# visitor's browser. It used to post to our own /api/enquiry relay, but
# Web3Forms rate-limits by source IP and the relay's Cloudflare IP is shared
# with a great many other sites, so it was refused 429 on first real use.
# Everything else is still this origin only.

# Fingerprinted build assets never change under the same name, so they can be
# cached forever.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# HTML must not be cached: it is how a publish reaches a returning visitor.
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
